{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"body":"## Investigation (2026-11-01) — mechanism located; fix needs a design decision\n\n**Mechanism.** The foreign load is the linked-worktree *store-mount* path, not ticket resolution. Stack captured at the warning:\n`_main_dispatch -> ensure_store_mounted_best_effort (_cli/_init.py) -> pending_init_is_symlink -> _main_worktree_tracker (_commands/init.py) -> tracker_dir(<main worktree path>) -> load_config(<main root>)`.\n`_main_worktree_tracker` takes the first `git worktree list --porcelain` entry (the main checkout) and calls `tracker_dir()` on it, which does a full `load_config` of the main checkout's `rebar.toml` (all layers validated, so its unknown keys warn) only to read `tracker.dir`.\n\n**Measured scope (fresh worktree at origin/main 4b74c52b378).**\n- Fires only while `.tickets-tracker` is absent, i.e. the first command in a new worktree. Both `list --status=open` and `show <id>` warn on that first run; the earlier table's \"list: no\" reflects run order (show had already created the symlink). With the symlink present: 0 main-config loads on 6 of 7 reruns; 1 rerun right after the first mount also loaded it once (not explained).\n- Instrumenting `_discover_project_config`: every other discovery in the command resolves to the worktree's `rebar.toml`. The main config's values are used for `tracker.dir` only; `load_config` caches by root, so they do not leak into the worktree's settings.\n- Not caused by 39821ae000a: the tree at `39821ae000a^` emits the same warning on first mount. The call has been there since d06b1020572 (2026-06-23, task 3e28-f913-d06b-471a), which deliberately routed the \"main worktree tracker path\" resolver through `tracker_dir()` so a custom `tracker.dir` is honoured.\n\n**AC3 (MCP stale-store).** Not this root cause: `pending_init_is_symlink` returns False unless `.git` is a file (linked worktree), and the main checkout's `.git` is a directory, so a server running from the main checkout never takes this path. The DIVERGED/stale-store symptom matches open bug b2e3-2fc3-523f-443a; not verified as identical."},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1793532689404888001,"uuid":"6a325723-6324-4d94-b5c5-c7284b887ded"}